      "message": "The commit message states:\n\"blk_mq_insert_request() takes the q-\u003eelevator path which asserts WARN_ON_ONCE(rq-\u003etag !\u003d BLK_MQ_NO_TAG) and then hands the request to the scheduler\u0027s insert_requests op.\"\n\nThere is no WARN_ON_ONCE(rq-\u003etag !\u003d BLK_MQ_NO_TAG) in blk_mq_insert_request() in the ACK tree. The actual stall occurs because bypassing hctx-\u003edispatch breaks the hardware queue restart / wakeup synchronization (smp_mb() paired with blk_mq_sched_restart(), SCHED_RESTART, and driver tag waitqueue wakeups). The commit message should be updated to accurately describe the queue stall mechanism.",
