      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, you\u0027re right on both counts. The earlier message was inaccurate.\n\nI confirmed against the source that blk_mq_insert_request() has no\nWARN_ON_ONCE(rq-\u003etag !\u003d BLK_MQ_NO_TAG) in this tree, and that the real\nstall is the loss of the hctx-\u003edispatch + SCHED_RESTART restart\nhandshake, not any tag-invariant violation. I\u0027ve reworded the commit\nmessage accordingly: the requeued work must land on hctx-\u003edispatch so\nthat the smp_mb() after the requeue (paired with the one in\n__blk_mq_sched_restart()) orders the addition against the SCHED_RESTART\ncheck; routing it through blk_mq_insert_request() (sw queue / elevator)\nbypasses that, so the queue is never rerun and the requests are never\nre-dispatched -\u003e stall.\n\nBRs,zhipeng",
